   "source": [
    "# Real-Time Fraud Detection: Threshold & Cost Optimization\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. Why `p >= 0.5` is Inappropriate for Fraud Detection\n",
    "In classical balanced binary classification, 0.5 is the intuitive decision boundary.\n",
    "However, in fraud detection:\n",
    "1. **Asymmetric Error Costs**: A false negative (missing a fraud attack) costs \$250 in average unrecoverable chargebacks, whereas a false positive (customer SMS confirmation / manual review) costs \$25 in operational friction.\n",
    "2. **Operational Triage**: Production risk engines route transactions into three operational buckets:\n",
    "   - **APPROVE**: Low risk, seamless user checkout.\n",
    "   - **REVIEW**: Elevated risk, queued for step-up multi-factor authentication (MFA) or human analyst inspection.\n",
    "   - **DECLINE**: High risk, outright transaction refusal to prevent fraud loss.\n",
    "\n",
    "In this notebook, we systematically optimize the decision thresholds against empirical validation data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.data.loader import load_credit_card_data\n",
    "from src.data.split import time_based_split\n",
    "from src.decision_engine.threshold import optimize_thresholds\n",
    "from src.decision_engine.cost_model import CostModel\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load trained calibrated model & feature engineer\n",
    "fe = joblib.load('../models/artifacts/feature_engineer.joblib')\n",
    "model = joblib.load('../models/artifacts/best_model.joblib')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load validation set\n",
    "df = load_credit_card_data('../data/raw/creditcard.csv')\n",
    "_, val_df, _ = time_based_split(df, val_size=0.15, test_size=0.15)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_val = fe.transform(val_df.drop(columns=['Class']))\n",
    "y_val = val_df['Class'].values\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predict calibrated probabilities\n",
    "val_probs = model.predict_proba(X_val)[:, 1]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Run threshold optimization\n",
    "opt_results = optimize_thresholds(y_val, val_probs, fp_cost=25.0, fn_cost=250.0)\n",
    "curve_df = opt_results['threshold_curve']\n",
    "recs = opt_results['recommendations']\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"=== Recommended Operational Thresholds ===\")\n",
    "for k, v in recs.items():\n",
    "    print(f\"  {k}: {v}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Visualizing Threshold vs Performance Metrics & Cost\n",
    "Examining how shifting the threshold impacts Precision, Recall, F1, and Total Financial Cost."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(15, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Precision, Recall, and F1 across thresholds\n",
    "axes[0].plot(curve_df['threshold'], curve_df['precision'], label='Precision', color='#2b5c8f', lw=2)\n",
    "axes[0].plot(curve_df['threshold'], curve_df['recall'], label='Recall', color='#d9534f', lw=2)\n",
    "axes[0].plot(curve_df['threshold'], curve_df['f1'], label='F1-Score', color='#5cb85c', lw=2, linestyle='--')\n",
    "axes[0].axvline(recs['f1_optimal_threshold'], color='green', linestyle=':', label=f\"F1 Optimal ({recs['f1_optimal_threshold']:.2f})\")\n",
    "axes[0].set_xlabel('Decision Threshold', fontsize=11)\n",
    "axes[0].set_ylabel('Metric Value', fontsize=11)\n",
    "axes[0].set_title('Precision, Recall & F1 Trade-off vs Threshold', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "axes[0].legend(loc='center left')\n",
    "axes[0].grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Financial Cost Curve\n",
    "axes[1].plot(curve_df['threshold'], curve_df['total_cost'], color='#d9534f', lw=2.5, label='Total Expected Loss ($)')\n",
    "axes[1].axvline(recs['cost_optimal_threshold'], color='red', linestyle='--', label=f\"Cost Optimal ({recs['cost_optimal_threshold']:.2f})\")\n",
    "axes[1].axvline(recs['recommended_review_threshold'], color='orange', linestyle=':', label=f\"Review Threshold ({recs['recommended_review_threshold']:.2f})\")\n",
    "axes[1].axvline(recs['recommended_decline_threshold'], color='purple', linestyle=':', label=f\"Decline Threshold ({recs['recommended_decline_threshold']:.2f})\")\n",
    "axes[1].set_xlabel('Decision Threshold', fontsize=11)\n",
    "axes[1].set_ylabel('Total Financial Cost ($)', fontsize=11)\n",
    "axes[1].set_title('Expected Financial Cost ($) vs Decision Threshold', fontsize=13, fontweight='bold')\n",
    "axes[1].legend(loc='upper right')\n",
    "axes[1].grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  }
